# L §4.6 step 2: "a row that says replace wins on its span over the rows known before it; a later row that overlaps
# an earlier-known row at the same keys without replace is refused at load (LOAD-OVERLAP)".  v2 replaces from
# 2026-07: 2 there, 1 before.  As known before v2, 1 everywhere: v1's open row read after that cut is held (L §8.2).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"

input n: int

version v1
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  n = 1

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-07..
  known 2026-06-01
  replace n = 2

ask q1: n law 2026-03-01
ask q2: n law 2026-08-01
ask q3: n law 2026-08-01 as known 2026-05-01
=== expect
q1: 1
  law date 2026-03-01, cut 2026-12-31
q2: 2
  law date 2026-08-01, cut 2026-12-31
q3: 1
  held: n = 1 (v1), read for 2026-08-01
  law date 2026-08-01, cut 2026-05-01
